Notes: Laps are read at one station (third train minus first), so neither the site, the distance nor
  the explosion time enters. The first and third trains travel the same way round, so the wind along
  the path is not cancelled as it is for Krakatoa's two directions. The printed distances and
  velocities used the radius of 1962 and serve only to check the transcription.

